diff --git a/common/foundation/produce/README.en.md b/common/foundation/produce/README.en.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e408b45
--- /dev/null
+++ b/common/foundation/produce/README.en.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# produce
+
+#### Description
+Produce is used for adapting production instructions and production aging on production versions, such as serial port transmission and parsing of production instructions.
+
+#### Directory Structure
+```
+/device/soc/hisilicon/common/foundation/produce
+├── include            # Header directory for utility functions
+└── src                # Implementation directory for utility functions
+```
+
+### Usage Guidelines
+1. Compile the production version for the first time on v352 using the command "./build.sh --product-name hispark_hi3751v352 --ccache --patch --gn-args selinux_adapter_enforce=false --gn-args production_construct_order_enable=true --gn-args production_construct_age_enable=true".
+2. For the first compilation of the production version on v900, use the command "./build.sh --product-name mp_ohos --ccache --patch --gn-args selinux_adapter_enforce=false --gn-args production_construct_order_enable=true --gn-args production_construct_age_enable=true".
+3. The production version of Selinux is turned off and the produce_server starts automatically upon startup. Regularly check the serial port for data transmission and reception.
\ No newline at end of file
